      "worked": "A radius is perpendicular to its tangent, so $OA\\perp AP$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}AP&=\\sqrt{(2r)^2-r^2}\\\\AP&=\\sqrt3r\\\\\\cos\\angle AOP&=\\frac{r}{2r}\\\\\\cos\\angle AOP&=\\frac12\\\\\\angle AOP&=\\frac\\pi3\\end{align*}$$\n\nBy symmetry, $OP$ bisects $\\angle AOB$. Subtract sector $OAB$ from quadrilateral $OAPB$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle AOB&=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\\\A_{OAPB}&=2\\times\\frac12r(\\sqrt3r)\\\\A_{OAPB}&=\\sqrt3r^2\\\\A_{\\text{shaded}}&=\\sqrt3r^2-\\frac12r^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\right)\\\\A_{\\text{shaded}}&=r^2\\left(\\sqrt3-\\frac\\pi3\\right)\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe area is in square units.",
